Hipfort part :
==============
1)  compile hipfort:
a) edit compile-hipfort.sh and change the path where to install hipfort
b) run ./compile-hipfort.sh

2) test the hipfort installation
a) edit compile-test-hipfort.sh and modify ROOT_HIPFORT to the path where hipfort has been installed
b) run ./compile-test-hipfort.sh
c) edit job_hipfort.sh and modify the --account project
d) run sbatch job_hipfort.sh
e) check-out the output typing tail slurm-*.out which should give
-- Running test 'vecadd' (Fortran 2008 interfaces)- device: AMD Instinct MI250X -  PASSED!

Notice that in compile-test-hipfort.sh, you can see the needed flags for compiling cpp and f90 files and for linking object files.

Elmer part :
============
1) kernel file : kernelPoisson.cpp
compile it typing
hipcc -fno-gpu-rdc -fPIC --offload-arch=gfx90a -c kernelPoisson.cpp

2) fortran interface : fortran_hip_interface.F90
compile it typing 
gfortran-13 -cpp -I$ROOT_HIPFORT/include/hipfort/amdgcn -c fortran_hip_interface.F90

3) Poisson solver modified with hip kernel call : Poisson.F90
compile it typing
gfortran-13 -cpp -I$ROOT_HIPFORT/include/hipfort/amdgcn -c Poisson.F90

final link : 
OBJS=*.o
gfortran-13 $OBJS -L$ROOT_HIPFORT/lib -lhipfort-amdgcn -L$ROCM_PATH/lib -lamdhip64 -Wl,-rpath=$ROCM_PATH/lib  -lstdc++ -o main_bin
